[{:db/id "q-337223/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "f5ea762f-3e61-5622-b6da-c96293f6ff9c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337223/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "dd840250-49fa-5551-b384-1fa1c40fec2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337223/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "11ddbceb-6b4b-5765-916d-c745dbb9d56c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337223/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "bfc513d0-eec4-5bd7-ac02-278bc05e2776" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337223/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "7b5ee0f6-499e-53b0-9a70-afc0bad17c86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337223/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "908e7516-da91-5c7c-9fa1-35a431b67efa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337223/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-337223/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-337223/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-337223/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-337223/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-337223/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337223" :question/id #uuid "103caf7c-e81f-5080-9c10-df7884ea851f" :question/math-academy-id "q-337223" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a d'Alembert differential equation?\n\n- $y=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{′})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+({y}^{′})^{2})$\n- $y{y}^{′}={x}^{3}y+1$\n- $y-x({y}^{′})^{2}+{e}^{{y}^{′}}=0$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nNote that, in the special case where $f({y}^{′})={y}^{′},$ the equation reduces to a Clairaut differential equation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a d'Alembert differential equation of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with \n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{′}),\\,g({y}^{′})=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+({y}^{′})^{2}).\n$$\n\n- Equation II is *not* a d'Alembert differential equation. Solving for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}-{x}^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhich cannot be written in the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}).$\n\n- Equation III is a d'Alembert differential equation. Isolating the variable $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=x({y}^{′})^{2}-{e}^{{y}^{′}},\n$$\n\nwhich is of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337223/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e69075-ef65-5a18-b911-601b515a9a84"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337223"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337226/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "0161dc5c-710d-5acf-ae81-da5f1c9e9901" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337226/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "aa6965db-fcda-5bb7-a109-01f94340593d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337226/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "cab1b8fa-53bc-5e22-846f-72b2eb74af69" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337226/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "4502525a-674f-5811-b2b4-178c481b1e2a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337226/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "d0c15830-2969-55fa-8ea0-507db94b1743" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337226/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ce10c5a-d986-517d-9ca6-37e4445da471" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337226/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-337226/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-337226/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-337226/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-337226/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-337226/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337226" :question/id #uuid "ffbf0fc3-7776-519a-bdcb-35221539c005" :question/math-academy-id "q-337226" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a d'Alembert differential equation?\n\n- $y=x({y}^{′})^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{′})$\n- $y+x({y}^{′})^{2}={2}^{{y}^{′}}$\n- $y{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y+x$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nNote that, in the special case where $f({y}^{′})={y}^{′},$ the equation reduces to a Clairaut differential equation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a d'Alembert differential equation of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with\n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=({y}^{′})^{2},\\,g({y}^{′})=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{′}).\n$$\n\n- Equation II is a d'Alembert differential equation. Isolating the variable $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=-x({y}^{′})^{2}+{2}^{{y}^{′}},\n$$\n\nwhich is a d'Alembert differential equation of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with \n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=-({y}^{′})^{2},\\,g({y}^{′})={2}^{{y}^{′}}.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is *not* a d'Alembert differential equation. Solving for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{{y}^{′}-{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhich cannot be written in the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337226/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e69075-ef65-5a18-b911-601b515a9a84"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337226"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337233/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "aa26ec4a-cea3-5e34-9982-8541822057ae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337233/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d5f49368-dab2-50c2-b5eb-4a88b83f483b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337233/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "8ebcd1e2-ae77-5c9e-994f-647d591477a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337233/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "787848c4-c2a4-5966-b61c-6a87a94fa0c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337233/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "9f92af6e-0847-527d-b2ca-16024916e1c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337233/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "140fbda9-3525-5582-a87b-3176bdcb1550" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337233/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-337233/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-337233/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-337233/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-337233/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-337233/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337233" :question/id #uuid "321dd86d-0a40-5d2e-8a10-ba07405bbb7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-337233" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a d'Alembert differential equation?\n\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{y}$\n- $y+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{′})={e}^{{y}^{′}}$\n- $y=x({y}^{′})^{3}+\\sqrt{1+({y}^{′})^{2}}$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nNote that, in the special case where $f({y}^{′})={y}^{′},$ the equation reduces to a Clairaut differential equation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is *not* a d'Alembert differential equation. Solving for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{y}^{′}-{x}^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhich cannot be written in the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}).$\n\n- Equation II is a d'Alembert differential equation. Isolating the variable $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny={e}^{{y}^{′}}-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhich is of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with\n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{′}),\\,g({y}^{′})={e}^{{y}^{′}}.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is a d'Alembert differential equation of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with\n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=({y}^{′})^{3},\\,g({y}^{′})=\\sqrt{1+({y}^{′})^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337233/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e69075-ef65-5a18-b911-601b515a9a84"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337233"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337229/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "b1554d4d-6231-5483-8feb-525585d54593" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337229/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "3647616c-3000-5179-ab34-0152325ff7dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337229/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "7286b900-9738-50b6-b6a3-e054d4b39ef8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337229/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "42be0dcf-ae61-5dff-95ea-81dd5285b7f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337229/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "1d096adf-7023-5a7c-b2d7-a0d1e3708270" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337229/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5174e357-d5fd-5d07-9f18-64e60d236a0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337229/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-337229/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-337229/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-337229/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-337229/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-337229/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337229" :question/id #uuid "689313e4-b91b-5057-8ee8-cd90bdff6367" :question/math-academy-id "q-337229" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a d'Alembert differential equation?\n\n- $y{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y+x$\n- $y+x({y}^{′})^{2}={e}^{{y}^{′}}$\n- $y=x({y}^{′})^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{′})$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nNote that, in the special case where $f({y}^{′})={y}^{′},$ the equation reduces to a Clairaut differential equation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is *not* a d'Alembert differential equation. Solving for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{{y}^{′}-{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhich cannot be written in the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}).$\n\n- Equation II is a d'Alembert differential equation. Isolating the variable $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny={e}^{{y}^{′}}-x({y}^{′})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich is of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with\n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=-({y}^{′})^{2},\\,g({y}^{′})={e}^{{y}^{′}}.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is a d'Alembert differential equation of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with\n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=({y}^{′})^{2},\\,g({y}^{′})=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{′}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337229/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e69075-ef65-5a18-b911-601b515a9a84"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337229"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337245/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "4087ae8f-e4c4-52b7-a676-0e5cffa7a713" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337245/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "585bc6ac-a0d3-5674-b2ac-1ecf4c39fcba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337245/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "13d0a54b-0d01-56a9-af31-dea9a1a2927c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337245/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "33e3edb9-eb8e-5609-9d07-7bdbb9111871" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337245/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "80a21573-def3-58cd-b469-647b60ac2071" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337245/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f62bd3f4-79a5-5edb-b1bb-551afd3c5a34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337245/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-337245/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-337245/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-337245/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-337245/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-337245/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337245" :question/id #uuid "7bfc3db0-28f4-5f5c-883d-a74f90abd3ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-337245" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a d'Alembert differential equation?\n\n- $y=x({y}^{′})^{3}+({y}^{′})^{2}$\n- $y-x\\sqrt{1+{y}^{′}}+\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{′}}=0$\n- ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{y}$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nNote that, in the special case where $f({y}^{′})={y}^{′},$ the equation reduces to a Clairaut differential equation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a d'Alembert differential equation of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with \n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=({y}^{′})^{3},\\,g({y}^{′})=({y}^{′})^{2}.\n$$\n\n- Equation II is a d'Alembert differential equation. Isolating the variable $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=x\\sqrt{1+{y}^{′}}-\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{′}},\n$$\n\nwhich is of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}).$\n\n- Equation III is *not* a d'Alembert differential equation. Solving for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}-{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhich cannot be written in the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337245/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e69075-ef65-5a18-b911-601b515a9a84"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337245"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365373/field-1/6b5a3a25e7a7bac75948e98b4b4715e94fde5a111a3d6a494d4d66066f7e87f7" :answer/id #uuid "bbf017d2-f4ac-5eb7-b7fb-1563031943b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t(t-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365373/field-1/c7ceb9c7f4281f7d474d2b565ab560d18188959bff80de8f97b53bc8f87be516" :answer/id #uuid "70c3bb7a-d2de-5ceb-a75c-313f7513639d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365373/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" :answer/id #uuid "d601e62f-ebc7-58e0-aead-1cc4435c308f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365373/field-1/5d7b2bec106062d1cf193353138e24aaf4abeaa38e62b37806f6889700b26bf5" :answer/id #uuid "627c361e-eb2b-5682-88df-0bc010cde681" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-2}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365373/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "24efc0c3-9c16-571a-941e-c4438c2041b5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365373/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-365373/field-1/6b5a3a25e7a7bac75948e98b4b4715e94fde5a111a3d6a494d4d66066f7e87f7" "q-365373/field-1/c7ceb9c7f4281f7d474d2b565ab560d18188959bff80de8f97b53bc8f87be516" "q-365373/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" "q-365373/field-1/5d7b2bec106062d1cf193353138e24aaf4abeaa38e62b37806f6889700b26bf5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365373/field-2/8ea445c44903d3856132beba39cf34c1891f46bd59a09efc52ecfb87e61f683a" :answer/id #uuid "6139c3ff-61e3-54c5-a306-8389f933935b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365373/field-2/3d9398572934089c3962473523263c547cfa4f2ff32c6c641242ca9aa32c98c0" :answer/id #uuid "ad8ec387-74cf-5ba5-a52f-5e95ec87ac3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-1}{t(t-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365373/field-2/6373709be4f5641308240b81f79bcbaf4b1941f9ba65a4040a5d0da432adc03a" :answer/id #uuid "9c08e7b4-6b84-5f60-96d2-368471e33e60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t(t-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365373/field-2/6b5a3a25e7a7bac75948e98b4b4715e94fde5a111a3d6a494d4d66066f7e87f7" :answer/id #uuid "b8ef3702-cdad-5a57-b5b8-ee2a3a515ca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t(t-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365373/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "244ca02e-9d4e-53be-a4ea-59cf3f7a4308" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365373/field-2/6373709be4f5641308240b81f79bcbaf4b1941f9ba65a4040a5d0da432adc03a" :answer-field/choices ["q-365373/field-2/8ea445c44903d3856132beba39cf34c1891f46bd59a09efc52ecfb87e61f683a" "q-365373/field-2/3d9398572934089c3962473523263c547cfa4f2ff32c6c641242ca9aa32c98c0" "q-365373/field-2/6373709be4f5641308240b81f79bcbaf4b1941f9ba65a4040a5d0da432adc03a" "q-365373/field-2/6b5a3a25e7a7bac75948e98b4b4715e94fde5a111a3d6a494d4d66066f7e87f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365373" :question/id #uuid "2306e9be-a7c2-54a3-8745-8c6e47c3ddd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-365373" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation, defined for $t>0:$\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nUsing the substitution $t=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ the equation can be transformed to a first-order linear equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the functions $P$ and $Q.$\n\n$\\,\\,P(t)=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,Q(t)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nIn our case, we wish to transform the equation\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\ninto a first-order linear equation for $x=x(t).$ We proceed in three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Substitute, and differentiate with respect to $x.$\n\nWe have the substitution\n\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=x{t}^{2}-t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating both sides with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x{t}^{2}-t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum and product rules and using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x{t}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(t) \\\\ t & ={t}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({t}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(t) \\\\ t & ={t}^{2}+2xt\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Isolate the derivative and take its reciprocal.\n\nWe isolate $\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-{t}^{2} & =2xt\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ t(1-t) & =(2xt-1)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{t(1-t)}{2xt-1} & =\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{t(1-t)}{2xt-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by taking the reciprocal of each side, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{2xt-1}{t(1-t)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Express the derivative as a first-order linear equation.\n\nFinally, we write this in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{2xt-1}{t(1-t)} \\\\ t(1-t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =2xt-1 \\\\ t(1-t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-2xt & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{2xt}{t(1-t)} & =\\frac{-1}{t(1-t)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{2x}{1-t} & =\\frac{-1}{t(1-t)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1} & =\\frac{1}{t(t-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{2}{t-1},\\,Q(t)=\\frac{1}{t(t-1)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365373/field-1" "q-365373/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126ffd6c-f5a9-564f-935f-398a126d2cbd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365373"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365376/field-1/ce5a3e8b7acf3b3582bdfc951f090929d26c0c7f83f5529e9dc29a52456ca171" :answer/id #uuid "09e2a8bf-a0d4-513c-88f2-2c1762a15908" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365376/field-1/dd37e628956d9e28d28f5dc0915bacf53c5f0bad20b597f00769e5acad9acb48" :answer/id #uuid "db17ec7e-82e3-5d4c-a5e3-00d4944e0790" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}{t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365376/field-1/0631ff4eaec97080eb6f46579145388c51302316765f71b4b0b9691072c8f6de" :answer/id #uuid "49af3203-42aa-50a9-ab67-dfbbb2341b83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365376/field-1/254ec71ee9cdf246e6933a953b2d0d4d3f33a6e30c43be4dd5cf81db21933f8d" :answer/id #uuid "85a43c0e-3328-51da-b549-60d9765c67a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365376/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8275f8bf-4ef9-591b-9984-460c9a71b9e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365376/field-1/ce5a3e8b7acf3b3582bdfc951f090929d26c0c7f83f5529e9dc29a52456ca171" :answer-field/choices ["q-365376/field-1/ce5a3e8b7acf3b3582bdfc951f090929d26c0c7f83f5529e9dc29a52456ca171" "q-365376/field-1/dd37e628956d9e28d28f5dc0915bacf53c5f0bad20b597f00769e5acad9acb48" "q-365376/field-1/0631ff4eaec97080eb6f46579145388c51302316765f71b4b0b9691072c8f6de" "q-365376/field-1/254ec71ee9cdf246e6933a953b2d0d4d3f33a6e30c43be4dd5cf81db21933f8d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365376/field-2/8ea445c44903d3856132beba39cf34c1891f46bd59a09efc52ecfb87e61f683a" :answer/id #uuid "4540c63d-ce2a-5f1e-bb52-9d8d80dd9085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365376/field-2/7cd3d1a34239b30e2deb801cac0c0748f6a71f64d3396514faa02b0bb8542bca" :answer/id #uuid "2b95c0ca-ad09-539f-bc7f-7af83d9e8a5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365376/field-2/dd37e628956d9e28d28f5dc0915bacf53c5f0bad20b597f00769e5acad9acb48" :answer/id #uuid "3a60d147-ee75-5e9f-a0ae-45c370eb7da3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}{t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365376/field-2/19ec682577bc201958556cdcce989bb6696f101dd89c4e38f29896617b96d568" :answer/id #uuid "4caaae79-6647-586e-9904-52a49f8c60d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365376/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b336962d-d025-5063-89fa-07abe2eb229c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365376/field-2/19ec682577bc201958556cdcce989bb6696f101dd89c4e38f29896617b96d568" :answer-field/choices ["q-365376/field-2/8ea445c44903d3856132beba39cf34c1891f46bd59a09efc52ecfb87e61f683a" "q-365376/field-2/7cd3d1a34239b30e2deb801cac0c0748f6a71f64d3396514faa02b0bb8542bca" "q-365376/field-2/dd37e628956d9e28d28f5dc0915bacf53c5f0bad20b597f00769e5acad9acb48" "q-365376/field-2/19ec682577bc201958556cdcce989bb6696f101dd89c4e38f29896617b96d568"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365376" :question/id #uuid "150152c9-bc0a-5dc6-b37c-9bddd7008264" :question/math-academy-id "q-365376" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=xsin\\,(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the substitution $t=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ the equation can be transformed to a first-order linear equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the functions $P$ and $Q.$\n\n$\\,\\,P(t)=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,Q(t)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nIn our case, we wish to transform the equation\n\n$$\ny=xsin\\,(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\ninto a first-order linear equation for $x=x(t).$ We proceed in three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Substitute, and differentiate with respect to $x.$\n\nWe have the substitution\n\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating both sides with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum and product rules and using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(t) \\\\ t & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(t) \\\\ t & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Isolate the derivative and take its reciprocal.\n\nWe isolate $\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & =(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+1)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+1} & =\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by taking the reciprocal of each side, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+1}{t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Express the derivative as a first-order linear equation.\n\nFinally, we write this in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+1}{t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)} \\\\ (t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+1 \\\\ (t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}{t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)} & =\\frac{1}{t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-t} & =\\frac{1}{t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-t},\\,Q(t)=\\frac{1}{t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365376/field-1" "q-365376/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126ffd6c-f5a9-564f-935f-398a126d2cbd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365376"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365332/field-1/19cff54c3752b756bcb3d8cdbdd10776351f5e690eba826b6140548e4c3f8637" :answer/id #uuid "9d8511f6-b720-522d-9040-efc7a18dc15f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365332/field-1/6a6c2f94544dbe6764d223ea6914af64d725a4a61f36abcfe75835439a414977" :answer/id #uuid "48be27cd-e17f-569a-a557-2f25b2fa8d2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365332/field-1/6373709be4f5641308240b81f79bcbaf4b1941f9ba65a4040a5d0da432adc03a" :answer/id #uuid "006c8ac8-966c-526e-811b-0349c9de1812" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t(t-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365332/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" :answer/id #uuid "12a52341-b0c9-52fd-a097-edecf8b68331" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365332/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0b321ee-223c-5c04-88d7-787e60bd30e0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365332/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-365332/field-1/19cff54c3752b756bcb3d8cdbdd10776351f5e690eba826b6140548e4c3f8637" "q-365332/field-1/6a6c2f94544dbe6764d223ea6914af64d725a4a61f36abcfe75835439a414977" "q-365332/field-1/6373709be4f5641308240b81f79bcbaf4b1941f9ba65a4040a5d0da432adc03a" "q-365332/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365332/field-2/1cefbdc64370ed55a90b5cf2ede144358f69d2ed177dc8aaa3af711d5e936c74" :answer/id #uuid "ecafe733-668f-51c0-9547-88b3439786f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t(1-t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365332/field-2/eefa1881bbf5184a173348e72d5e3a379c15714750b16be7374cb6c7cb2c544c" :answer/id #uuid "7726bfda-8fb8-5e8e-9f6c-c000c4d319e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t(1-t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365332/field-2/8ea445c44903d3856132beba39cf34c1891f46bd59a09efc52ecfb87e61f683a" :answer/id #uuid "a11e37b3-4c53-5215-8cf7-fddfcef86c09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365332/field-2/285d3f19fe6d1381c6d92af29428952b715d9d44d10928529500246c93d2f855" :answer/id #uuid "bb4898a4-5d7f-5025-880e-52b6e27d2254" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t(2-t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365332/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2be8351f-4fe0-53c1-9b6d-03664ed23c7f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365332/field-2/1cefbdc64370ed55a90b5cf2ede144358f69d2ed177dc8aaa3af711d5e936c74" :answer-field/choices ["q-365332/field-2/1cefbdc64370ed55a90b5cf2ede144358f69d2ed177dc8aaa3af711d5e936c74" "q-365332/field-2/eefa1881bbf5184a173348e72d5e3a379c15714750b16be7374cb6c7cb2c544c" "q-365332/field-2/8ea445c44903d3856132beba39cf34c1891f46bd59a09efc52ecfb87e61f683a" "q-365332/field-2/285d3f19fe6d1381c6d92af29428952b715d9d44d10928529500246c93d2f855"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365332" :question/id #uuid "3c993f1a-3881-5577-a63a-84f119de18f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-365332" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation, defined for $t>0:$\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nUsing the substitution $t=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ the equation can be transformed to a first-order linear equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the functions $P$ and $Q.$\n\n$\\,\\,P(t)=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,Q(t)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nIn our case, we wish to transform the equation\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\ninto a first-order linear equation for $x=x(t).$ We proceed in three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Substitute, and differentiate with respect to $x.$\n\nWe have the substitution\n\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=x{t}^{2}+t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating both sides with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x{t}^{2}+t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum and product rules and using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x{t}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(t) \\\\ t & ={t}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({t}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(t) \\\\ t & ={t}^{2}+2xt\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Isolate the derivative and take its reciprocal.\n\nWe isolate $\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-{t}^{2} & =2xt\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ t(1-t) & =(2xt+1)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{t(1-t)}{2xt+1} & =\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{t(1-t)}{2xt+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by taking the reciprocal of each side, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{2xt+1}{t(1-t)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Express the derivative as a first-order linear equation.\n\nFinally, we write this in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{2xt+1}{t(1-t)} \\\\ t(1-t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =2xt+1 \\\\ t(1-t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-2xt & =1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{2xt}{t(1-t)} & =\\frac{1}{t(1-t)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{2x}{1-t} & =\\frac{1}{t(1-t)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1} & =\\frac{1}{t(1-t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{2}{t-1},\\,Q(t)=\\frac{1}{t(1-t)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365332/field-1" "q-365332/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126ffd6c-f5a9-564f-935f-398a126d2cbd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365332"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365383/field-1/6373709be4f5641308240b81f79bcbaf4b1941f9ba65a4040a5d0da432adc03a" :answer/id #uuid "9ad4c884-5086-5a77-8955-827336e1edc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t(t-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365383/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" :answer/id #uuid "025329f5-786c-5d12-ac51-c07e1a27b9ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365383/field-1/6a6c2f94544dbe6764d223ea6914af64d725a4a61f36abcfe75835439a414977" :answer/id #uuid "0d985ce9-1500-5408-8bc5-80ad6b4bc1bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365383/field-1/19cff54c3752b756bcb3d8cdbdd10776351f5e690eba826b6140548e4c3f8637" :answer/id #uuid "d388650f-b02b-5a36-b8aa-9463592f4e4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365383/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "83ceece8-8dac-5280-8c61-005296e37535" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365383/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-365383/field-1/6373709be4f5641308240b81f79bcbaf4b1941f9ba65a4040a5d0da432adc03a" "q-365383/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" "q-365383/field-1/6a6c2f94544dbe6764d223ea6914af64d725a4a61f36abcfe75835439a414977" "q-365383/field-1/19cff54c3752b756bcb3d8cdbdd10776351f5e690eba826b6140548e4c3f8637"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365383/field-2/3ad84b50a1b2671497179f897ae0a25f8e2b42b1532811503db528933d088349" :answer/id #uuid "8b6a39b7-1215-5669-960d-385ac94aba02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t(2-{t}^{2})}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365383/field-2/5d70b2820250203517b3c205c7aed942380a32c66d5f2b23c05b3fe9c705b24c" :answer/id #uuid "0922d9c5-754f-5a1e-8963-b88a6dffecba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t(1-{t}^{2})}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365383/field-2/e7becf0f574e48953ecd4e560c55679dd0fc5c7da6ffb8c617b65275965e2a73" :answer/id #uuid "83c1d9d7-076d-543d-9b17-4dc3b0d56544" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t(1-t)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365383/field-2/227fa7dd95ae696148a0be584023afad4b96837887aa1b0bce777e50676b1934" :answer/id #uuid "fa389b09-27e7-5d61-8dde-495e97b26b1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t(1-{t}^{2})}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365383/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d44a843e-36fb-5966-bd28-8d0d5ed0efc7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365383/field-2/227fa7dd95ae696148a0be584023afad4b96837887aa1b0bce777e50676b1934" :answer-field/choices ["q-365383/field-2/3ad84b50a1b2671497179f897ae0a25f8e2b42b1532811503db528933d088349" "q-365383/field-2/5d70b2820250203517b3c205c7aed942380a32c66d5f2b23c05b3fe9c705b24c" "q-365383/field-2/e7becf0f574e48953ecd4e560c55679dd0fc5c7da6ffb8c617b65275965e2a73" "q-365383/field-2/227fa7dd95ae696148a0be584023afad4b96837887aa1b0bce777e50676b1934"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365383" :question/id #uuid "83b1f29c-634d-560e-bd30-467a8e32d303" :question/math-academy-id "q-365383" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation, defined for $t>0:$\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+ln\\,(1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})\n$$\n\nUsing the substitution $t=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ the equation can be transformed to a first-order linear equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the functions $P$ and $Q.$\n\n$\\,\\,P(t)=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,Q(t)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nIn our case, we wish to transform the equation\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+ln\\,(1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})\n$$\n\ninto a first-order linear equation for $x=x(t).$ We proceed in three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Substitute, and differentiate with respect to $x.$\n\nWe have the substitution\n\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=x{t}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+t).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating both sides with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x{t}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum and product rules and using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x{t}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+t)) \\\\ t & ={t}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({t}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+t)) \\\\ t & ={t}^{2}+2xt\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{1+t}\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Isolate the derivative and take its reciprocal.\n\nWe isolate $\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-{t}^{2} & =2xt\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{1+t}\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ t(1-t) & =(2xt+\\frac{1}{1+t})\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{t(1-t)}{2xt+\\frac{1}{1+t}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{t(1-t)}{2xt+\\frac{1}{1+t}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by taking the reciprocal of each side, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{2xt+\\frac{1}{1+t}}{t(1-t)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Express the derivative as a first-order linear equation.\n\nFinally, we write this in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{2xt+\\frac{1}{1+t}}{t(1-t)} \\\\ t(1-t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =2xt+\\frac{1}{1+t} \\\\ t(1-t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-2xt & =\\frac{1}{1+t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{2xt}{t(1-t)} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{1+t}}{t(1-t)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{2x}{1-t} & =\\frac{1}{t(1-t)(1+t)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1} & =\\frac{1}{t(1-{t}^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{2}{t-1},\\,Q(t)=\\frac{1}{t(1-{t}^{2})}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365383/field-1" "q-365383/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126ffd6c-f5a9-564f-935f-398a126d2cbd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365383"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365386/field-1/808d71f8b24d0a6cd9321b0c93980be446904ab8a45b1ba1cbefbbe7cc58c4ff" :answer/id #uuid "ae7e8502-2426-59c9-b59e-7b16aa759857" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3t}{1-{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365386/field-1/b711cb444109e7f0802d0a5d5f21601b2356455c520ae0435a767c7b42c1602e" :answer/id #uuid "0b23941f-c760-546f-bff2-c9d3ee30cf71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365386/field-1/41ca4162a0167fd64dc13830e997c11a2fda6234f5cba2efce4ee44c3beb7410" :answer/id #uuid "bf7dc589-6712-5391-bbac-8429ea9bf09f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{{t}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365386/field-1/2207f915edb2b612422d64a5be9fd73593a736556e8b36268518a58640112f73" :answer/id #uuid "47129f3a-e474-59c8-99e3-63ba6a314a4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3t}{{t}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365386/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "63a6bf39-847c-589a-9371-27fe10d244a5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365386/field-1/2207f915edb2b612422d64a5be9fd73593a736556e8b36268518a58640112f73" :answer-field/choices ["q-365386/field-1/808d71f8b24d0a6cd9321b0c93980be446904ab8a45b1ba1cbefbbe7cc58c4ff" "q-365386/field-1/b711cb444109e7f0802d0a5d5f21601b2356455c520ae0435a767c7b42c1602e" "q-365386/field-1/41ca4162a0167fd64dc13830e997c11a2fda6234f5cba2efce4ee44c3beb7410" "q-365386/field-1/2207f915edb2b612422d64a5be9fd73593a736556e8b36268518a58640112f73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365386/field-2/06f8445457fe4755ede4e67bbd63b96013bafa770656ddaa702d54700bbbf175" :answer/id #uuid "0d9ede98-49b8-5d78-aa8f-b7b27b88cea9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365386/field-2/c33ac0dee092be8c3448898fdf1caba80ec1867b911120f413092c87da1da7ff" :answer/id #uuid "bb1dd85f-ca9e-5133-b05a-63b7ca9018c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{t}{1-{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365386/field-2/f6334ba432730723c9d8ba93fe647ef5f7684fa3f3e384b4c2bf793ede3323ef" :answer/id #uuid "fb269bb8-0a1e-5f1d-ab58-1818d33a3a69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1-{t}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365386/field-2/227fa7dd95ae696148a0be584023afad4b96837887aa1b0bce777e50676b1934" :answer/id #uuid "5ba30a04-aaf3-564e-8909-dc1cbf42e363" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t(1-{t}^{2})}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365386/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b184db88-2cf7-5efe-8b56-a13f2aac19ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365386/field-2/06f8445457fe4755ede4e67bbd63b96013bafa770656ddaa702d54700bbbf175" :answer-field/choices ["q-365386/field-2/06f8445457fe4755ede4e67bbd63b96013bafa770656ddaa702d54700bbbf175" "q-365386/field-2/c33ac0dee092be8c3448898fdf1caba80ec1867b911120f413092c87da1da7ff" "q-365386/field-2/f6334ba432730723c9d8ba93fe647ef5f7684fa3f3e384b4c2bf793ede3323ef" "q-365386/field-2/227fa7dd95ae696148a0be584023afad4b96837887aa1b0bce777e50676b1934"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365386" :question/id #uuid "655d56a0-a0fa-5054-8a82-3c774367f365" :question/math-academy-id "q-365386" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation, defined for $t>0:$\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{3}+ln\\,(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})\n$$\n\nUsing the substitution $t=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ the equation can be transformed to a first-order linear equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the functions $P$ and $Q.$\n\n$\\,\\,P(t)=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,Q(t)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nIn our case, we wish to transform the equation\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{3}+ln\\,(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})\n$$\n\ninto a first-order linear equation for $x=x(t).$ We proceed in three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Substitute, and differentiate with respect to $x.$\n\nWe have the substitution\n\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=x{t}^{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating both sides with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x{t}^{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum and product rules and using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x{t}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ t & ={t}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({t}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ t & ={t}^{3}+3x{t}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{t}\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Isolate the derivative and take its reciprocal.\n\nWe isolate $\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-{t}^{3} & =3x{t}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{t}\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ t(1-{t}^{2}) & =(\\frac{3x{t}^{3}+1}{t})\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{{t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})}{3x{t}^{3}+1} & =\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})}{3x{t}^{3}+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by taking the reciprocal of each side, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{3x{t}^{3}+1}{{t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Express the derivative as a first-order linear equation.\n\nFinally, we write this in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{3x{t}^{3}+1}{{t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})} \\\\ {t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =3x{t}^{3}+1 \\\\ {t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-3x{t}^{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{3x{t}^{3}}{{t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})} & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{3tx}{1-{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{3tx}{{t}^{2}-1} & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{3t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,Q(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365386/field-1" "q-365386/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126ffd6c-f5a9-564f-935f-398a126d2cbd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365386"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337727/selection/2601acdba8609a2a11052a4c929b9778e75f8f5e9a78628f44269818414996aa" :answer/id #uuid "f7b517ad-c08e-5682-b934-617f61c10ff7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{t}^{2}+t-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337727/selection/90754c008a85d0e2122fc4ad3d4c471ec83b0b9310e915682ee19b2ff3483cbd" :answer/id #uuid "e973b2d9-41fa-54df-ad5d-697fc7a97fe7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}+t+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337727/selection/9df3831a4ad2791ef6b732220cc763c57437e3ed0f7ee493b4e0e66a92363d1e" :answer/id #uuid "96c1956a-e826-5c35-896c-a9d87b4af763" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{t}^{2}-t+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337727/selection/443bcaae0eb99da04a4b4e260b6171476e4ec6242819920100bf50e8e32bd5c4" :answer/id #uuid "08929cf8-04b6-5dfc-84ef-dea55f47786e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{t}^{2}+t+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337727/selection/1eca15fdd50100d8e2efe4ebd9aa2e663e5121026ac42fc8b7e0be258b24a1da" :answer/id #uuid "bcc3e7b4-34b2-52db-b638-548c3e47a758" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}-t-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337727/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "884136c1-0552-5e75-a8ab-27e04fb189ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337727/selection/443bcaae0eb99da04a4b4e260b6171476e4ec6242819920100bf50e8e32bd5c4" :answer-field/choices ["q-337727/selection/2601acdba8609a2a11052a4c929b9778e75f8f5e9a78628f44269818414996aa" "q-337727/selection/90754c008a85d0e2122fc4ad3d4c471ec83b0b9310e915682ee19b2ff3483cbd" "q-337727/selection/9df3831a4ad2791ef6b732220cc763c57437e3ed0f7ee493b4e0e66a92363d1e" "q-337727/selection/443bcaae0eb99da04a4b4e260b6171476e4ec6242819920100bf50e8e32bd5c4" "q-337727/selection/1eca15fdd50100d8e2efe4ebd9aa2e663e5121026ac42fc8b7e0be258b24a1da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337727" :question/id #uuid "1ce78930-00d8-54c5-aa83-81d95802b525" :question/math-academy-id "q-337727" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2)-{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\ny(t)=(C{e}^{-t/2}+2t-4)f(t)+g(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find $f(t)+g(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{2}x=t.\n$$\n\n*You may also wish to make use of the following result (constants omitted):*\n\n$$\n\\int t{e}^{t/2}\\,\\text{d}t=(2t-4){e}^{t/2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{2}x=t.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{t/2} & =t{e}^{t/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t/2}) & =t{e}^{t/2} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t/2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int t{e}^{t/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x{e}^{t/2} & =(2t-4){e}^{t/2}+C \\\\ x & =2t-4+C{e}^{-t/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{-t/2}+2t-4.\n$$\n\nTo recover $y$, we substitute $x$ into\n\n$$\ny=x(t+2)-{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =(C{e}^{-t/2}+2t-4)(t+2)-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $f(t)=t+2,\\text{ }g(t)=-{t}^{2},$ and\n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)=-{t}^{2}+t+2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-337727/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6bb3f2e-ee56-56f2-94f2-4b454a187ab7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337727"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337864/selection/cb9ad14c4d0189695cf5d02baf58f5eec7ac941edc170f6dffed142cbab880f5" :answer/id #uuid "eb034691-5957-5401-8d17-3633ef30a615" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337864/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "b171348c-29b6-5a10-99b4-ea9e8c853e23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337864/selection/d037fb8cf08736501438259d060f65c7d8e4deabf8118415f202107f91c60ade" :answer/id #uuid "f509f735-91fe-5b12-baf3-c26186368d5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337864/selection/402698786a2196947323809d3a80b73a46d8692651fdfd7bfaed955c55f7637a" :answer/id #uuid "1ccbecb1-bab5-51a2-90cd-8f5f108862de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337864/selection/b77633b0368d8725fb5dcaece4aed8339ab5d3308acf6e8e6f2f935193fda378" :answer/id #uuid "dc15a156-b02c-5933-b4fd-6adc6acb8b63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337864/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bc299b1-4c30-5f28-933e-2028cd25eb8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337864/selection/b77633b0368d8725fb5dcaece4aed8339ab5d3308acf6e8e6f2f935193fda378" :answer-field/choices ["q-337864/selection/cb9ad14c4d0189695cf5d02baf58f5eec7ac941edc170f6dffed142cbab880f5" "q-337864/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-337864/selection/d037fb8cf08736501438259d060f65c7d8e4deabf8118415f202107f91c60ade" "q-337864/selection/402698786a2196947323809d3a80b73a46d8692651fdfd7bfaed955c55f7637a" "q-337864/selection/b77633b0368d8725fb5dcaece4aed8339ab5d3308acf6e8e6f2f935193fda378"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337864" :question/id #uuid "4b05fd8b-2a28-5543-b46b-05a4d23444e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-337864" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}-2{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\ny(t)=(\\frac{2{t}^{2}-4t+C}{(t-1)^{2}})f(t)+g(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find $f(t)+g(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{4}{t-1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{4}{t-1}.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2/(t-1)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t-1|} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =(t-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(t-1)^{2}\\frac{2x}{t-1} & =(t-1)^{2}\\frac{4}{t-1} \\\\ (t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x & =4(t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2}) & =4(t-1) \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 4(t-1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =\\int (4t-4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =2{t}^{2}-4t+C \\\\ x & =\\frac{2{t}^{2}-4t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{2{t}^{2}-4t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo recover $y$, we substitute $x$ into\n\n$$\ny=x{t}^{2}-2{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =(\\frac{2{t}^{2}-4t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}){t}^{2}-2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $f(t)={t}^{2},\\text{ }g(t)=-2{t}^{2},$ and\n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)=-{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-337864/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6bb3f2e-ee56-56f2-94f2-4b454a187ab7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337864"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337683/selection/7a9883688e5a79ab7968a3741ab5216a27163c10ffceeb2b4034b8e6ed3cd05c" :answer/id #uuid "81d62d7e-7928-5a76-a3c7-c37f3cd3af57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=\\frac{t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|}{(t-1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337683/selection/f0670fcfae6d3e3bc85ac1175407b6987a7a7cfd0b0ee6e8365e814c1257ca9f" :answer/id #uuid "88bca819-1653-5ebb-b415-904fd7ebaa4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=\\frac{t-1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|}{(t-1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337683/selection/46e8b1914acaa43b8d44cee3a7befbee69a49eaf0877aeccc17719d40f5de070" :answer/id #uuid "138259d3-557b-5b07-a772-9648d4b47a1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=\\frac{t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|}{(t-1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337683/selection/4f462cc4f62eafefaaad2511e55ad7b05ab58b9e41ed49da9a12aeba57d725e7" :answer/id #uuid "842f914d-046b-5192-af39-bb4c196c0bd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=\\frac{t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337683/selection/984cdc8537bf3ff61acae23e6ed01d183d79cf74a7e83ca48e0fc63f4d2dd3d1" :answer/id #uuid "d1257380-7e6d-5cfc-b3e1-03966eeb658b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=\\frac{t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|}{(t+1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337683/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a209e160-2816-572c-83d2-a9ea6e94cc56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337683/selection/7a9883688e5a79ab7968a3741ab5216a27163c10ffceeb2b4034b8e6ed3cd05c" :answer-field/choices ["q-337683/selection/7a9883688e5a79ab7968a3741ab5216a27163c10ffceeb2b4034b8e6ed3cd05c" "q-337683/selection/f0670fcfae6d3e3bc85ac1175407b6987a7a7cfd0b0ee6e8365e814c1257ca9f" "q-337683/selection/46e8b1914acaa43b8d44cee3a7befbee69a49eaf0877aeccc17719d40f5de070" "q-337683/selection/4f462cc4f62eafefaaad2511e55ad7b05ab58b9e41ed49da9a12aeba57d725e7" "q-337683/selection/984cdc8537bf3ff61acae23e6ed01d183d79cf74a7e83ca48e0fc63f4d2dd3d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337683" :question/id #uuid "2d13645f-14c8-548f-84bd-b0359fdd5dce" :question/math-academy-id "q-337683" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{C}{(t-1)^{2}}+f(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find the function $f(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2}{t-1}x=\\frac{1}{t(t-1)}.\n$$\n\n*You may also wish to make use of the following result (constants omitted):*\n\n$$\n\\int (1-\\frac{1}{t})\\,\\text{d}t=t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2}{t-1}x=\\frac{1}{t(t-1)}.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t),\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t}={e}^{\\int \\frac{2}{t-1}\\,\\text{d}t}={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t-1|}=(t-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x & =1-\\frac{1}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2}) & =1-\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int (1-\\frac{1}{t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|+C \\\\ x & =\\frac{C}{(t-1)^{2}}+\\frac{t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|}{(t-1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{C}{(t-1)^{2}}+\\frac{t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|}{(t-1)^{2}}\n$$\n\nand finally, $f(t)=\\frac{t-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|}{(t-1)^{2}}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337683/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6bb3f2e-ee56-56f2-94f2-4b454a187ab7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337683"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337721/selection/18ab0b820d984b5925872a870070de4240ccb342182a0423f4f6b064aeef3430" :answer/id #uuid "1b555bf5-8563-5912-b8aa-5092cc5c2456" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337721/selection/42c07b5dbc725e033b096c75aacfc497649fb4d587f9aee2552fc6486e3ab67d" :answer/id #uuid "957726a9-5399-5e2d-93c2-57d65d3a747c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}+2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337721/selection/75328594a229d685f32816ff6d35c76ed8c187f11052d8aeb14faebc02ec148a" :answer/id #uuid "de439b4c-1956-592d-9b4c-7639a4abeca0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}-2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337721/selection/5801bfe7187ffc56f8bb39405094b0a112228c285a505e02404b8a612daca879" :answer/id #uuid "96f62f42-15f4-507d-acec-0be367977493" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{t}^{2}-t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337721/selection/8558a106118069325df278009db882e0c9a7b3603a7405b79f4e03b682c1aeb6" :answer/id #uuid "9cba12c4-5017-5926-9ef7-0c178b5b1715" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{t}^{2}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337721/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcd69973-65c9-51e4-97b5-0155ee907745" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337721/selection/75328594a229d685f32816ff6d35c76ed8c187f11052d8aeb14faebc02ec148a" :answer-field/choices ["q-337721/selection/18ab0b820d984b5925872a870070de4240ccb342182a0423f4f6b064aeef3430" "q-337721/selection/42c07b5dbc725e033b096c75aacfc497649fb4d587f9aee2552fc6486e3ab67d" "q-337721/selection/75328594a229d685f32816ff6d35c76ed8c187f11052d8aeb14faebc02ec148a" "q-337721/selection/5801bfe7187ffc56f8bb39405094b0a112228c285a505e02404b8a612daca879" "q-337721/selection/8558a106118069325df278009db882e0c9a7b3603a7405b79f4e03b682c1aeb6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337721" :question/id #uuid "0c2b1c78-5509-5e6f-b887-46bb53bd6ea6" :question/math-academy-id "q-337721" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}-2(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}).\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\ny(t)=(\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-6t+{t}^{2}+C}{2(t-1)^{2}})f(t)+g(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find $f(t)+g(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{2-t}{t(1-t)}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{2-t}{t(1-t)}.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2/(t-1)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t-1|} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =(t-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x & =(t-1)^{2}\\frac{2-t}{t(1-t)} \\\\ (t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x & =\\frac{(1-t)(2-t)}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2}) & =\\frac{2-t}{t}(1-t) \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\frac{2-t}{t}(1-t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =\\int (\\frac{2}{t}-3+t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3t+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ x & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-6t+{t}^{2}+C}{2(t-1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-6t+{t}^{2}+C}{2(t-1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo recover $y$, we substitute $x$ into\n\n$$\ny=x{t}^{2}-2t,\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =(\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-6t+{t}^{2}+C}{2(t-1)^{2}}){t}^{2}-2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $f(t)={t}^{2},\\text{ }g(t)=-2t,$ and\n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)={t}^{2}-2t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-337721/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6bb3f2e-ee56-56f2-94f2-4b454a187ab7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337721"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337699/selection/0d3e8fbe9c12fc5f6b33502f780feec6c9a9aa3ff45bbb9e8655c65d30011ae9" :answer/id #uuid "30c20f35-ae3f-5da1-bb0c-f96b6c862d96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=4-3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337699/selection/5e5baf61f529fc636a4392ee9288313d22786a5144b2e7d1bfc112a9607b0b76" :answer/id #uuid "21a0589f-f6fe-56fb-9cbd-6f6facc6e6e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=4-t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337699/selection/6d2ed0948d98c634b66d93516ed2c22c5ef27d308a4b964a55839827e202d3f0" :answer/id #uuid "6e33fd0d-e752-50d1-ad81-d31d5112603d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=4+3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337699/selection/e93e6d8504a1af6d9e1622d453abca60b2a37e20359e09279985837baf0f1742" :answer/id #uuid "64734250-da3c-5d28-9449-083df2e2ad4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=3-4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337699/selection/6fd2a465c42941ee4760b0ee51ecb52849c6161d50c22488dd571cf0ebe6e3b6" :answer/id #uuid "20c9c7a0-92cf-54b1-ba4c-b1baed0794be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(t)=5-3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337699/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2752a01b-5638-5477-8e4e-774be2937898" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337699/selection/0d3e8fbe9c12fc5f6b33502f780feec6c9a9aa3ff45bbb9e8655c65d30011ae9" :answer-field/choices ["q-337699/selection/0d3e8fbe9c12fc5f6b33502f780feec6c9a9aa3ff45bbb9e8655c65d30011ae9" "q-337699/selection/5e5baf61f529fc636a4392ee9288313d22786a5144b2e7d1bfc112a9607b0b76" "q-337699/selection/6d2ed0948d98c634b66d93516ed2c22c5ef27d308a4b964a55839827e202d3f0" "q-337699/selection/e93e6d8504a1af6d9e1622d453abca60b2a37e20359e09279985837baf0f1742" "q-337699/selection/6fd2a465c42941ee4760b0ee51ecb52849c6161d50c22488dd571cf0ebe6e3b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337699" :question/id #uuid "e9151b70-2cb0-5312-ba19-ff72c23b0f47" :question/math-academy-id "q-337699" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x(1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})+\\frac{3}{2}{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{-t}+f(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find the function $f(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x=1-3t.\n$$\n\n*You may also wish to make use of the following result (constants omitted):*\n\n$$\n\\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t=(t-1){e}^{t}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x=1-3t.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t}={e}^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}t}={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x{e}^{t} & =(1-3t){e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t}) & =(1-3t){e}^{t} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int (1-3t){e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x{e}^{t} & =\\int (1-3t){e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x{e}^{t} & =\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t-3\\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x{e}^{t} & ={e}^{t}-3(t-1){e}^{t}+C \\\\ x & =4-3t+C{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{-t}+4-3t\n$$\n\nand finally, $f(t)=4-3t.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337699/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6bb3f2e-ee56-56f2-94f2-4b454a187ab7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337699"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21716"] :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a d'Alembert differential equation?\n\n- $yy' = x^2y + e^x$\n\n- $y = x\\ln(1+y') + (y')^2$\n\n- $y + \\dfrac{x}{1+y'} - y' = 0$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny = xf(y') + g(y'),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of $y'.$ \n\nNote that, in the special case where $f(y') = y',$ the equation reduces to a Clairaut differential equation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is *not* a d'Alembert differential equation. Solving for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{e^x}{y' - x^2},\n$$\n\nwhich cannot be written in the form $y = xf(y') + g(y').$\n\n- Equation II is a d'Alembert differential equation of the form $y = xf(y') + g(y')$ with\n\n$$\nf(y') = \\ln(1+y'), \\qquad g(y') = (y')^2.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is a d'Alembert differential equation. Isolating the variable $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny = y' - \\dfrac{x}{1+y'},\n$$\n\nwhich is of the form $y = xf(y') + g(y')$ with\n\n$$\nf(y') = -\\dfrac{1}{1+y'}, \\qquad g(y') = y'.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21773"] :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny = 2x\\sin\\!\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}\\right) + 5\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}\\right)^2.\n$$\n\nUsing the substitution $t = \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ the equation can be transformed to a first-order linear equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t} + P(t)x = Q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the functions $P$ and $Q.$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny = xf(y') + g(y'),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of $y'.$ \n\nIn our case, we wish to transform the equation\n\n$$\ny = 2x\\sin\\!\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}\\right) + 5\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}\\right)^2\n$$\n\ninto a first-order linear equation for $x = x(t).$ We proceed in three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Substitute, and differentiate with respect to $x.$\n\nWe have the substitution\n\n$$\nt = \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny = 2x\\sin t + 5t^2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating both sides with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+5{t}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum and product rules, and using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{t}^{2}) \\\\ t & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+10t\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ t & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+10t\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Isolate the derivative and take its reciprocal.\n\nWe isolate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d t}{\\textrm d x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & =(2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+10t)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+10t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d t}{\\textrm d x}=\\dfrac{t-2\\sin t}{2x\\cos t+10t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by taking the reciprocal of each side, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}=\\dfrac{2x\\cos t+10t}{t-2\\sin t}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Express the derivative as a first-order linear equation.\n\nFinally, we write this in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t} + P(t)x = Q(t)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+10t}{t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\ (t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+10t \\\\ (t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =10t \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}x & =\\frac{10t}{t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t}x & =\\frac{10t}{t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(t) = \\dfrac{2\\cos t}{2\\sin t-t}, \\qquad Q(t) = \\dfrac{10t}{t-2\\sin t}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21717"] :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny = x\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}-1\\right)^2 + 2\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}\\right).\n$$\n\nIf $y'(x) = t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t), y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\ny(t) = \\left( \\dfrac{2\\ln|t| - t^2+C}{2(t-1)^2} \\right) f(t) + g(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find $f(t)+g(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t} + \\dfrac{2x}{t-1} = \\frac{1+t}{t(1-t)}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny = xf(y') + g(y'),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of $y'.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution $y'(x) = t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t} + \\dfrac{2x}{t-1} = \\frac{1+t}{t(1-t)}.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t} + P(t)x = Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2/(t-1)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t-1|} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =(t-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x & =(t-1)^{2}\\frac{1+t}{t(1-t)} \\\\ (t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x & =\\frac{1-{t}^{2}}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2}) & =\\frac{1-{t}^{2}}{t} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\frac{1-{t}^{2}}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =\\int \\frac{1}{t}-t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ x & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-{t}^{2}+C}{2(t-1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t) = \\dfrac{2\\ln|t| - t^2+C}{2(t-1)^2}.\n$$\n\nTo recover $y$, we substitute $x$ into\n\n$$\ny = x(t-1)^2 + 2t,\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-{t}^{2}+C}{2(t-1)^{2}})(t-1)^{2}+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $f(t)=(t-1)^2,\\ g(t)=2t,$ and\n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t) = t^2 +1.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
